olution. C.E.W. is supported by the Swedish Heart Lung Foundation (HLF 2023-0463 and HLF 2021-0519), and the Swedish Research Council (2022-00796). N.J.W.R. is supported by MR/Y010736/1 from the Medical Research Council and IF\\R1\\231034 from the Royal Society. E.M. is supported in part by the intramural program Metabolomics and multi-omics (ZIC TR000547) at the National Center for Advancing Translational Sciences, part of the NIH. DNAm profiling of the Generation Scotland samples was carried out by the Genetics Core Laboratory at the Edinburgh Clinical Research Facility, University of Edinburgh and was funded by the Medical Research Council UK and Wellcome Trust (104036/Z/14/Z and 220857/Z/20/Z). Core support was received from the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government Health Directorates (CZD/16/6) and the Scottish Funding Council (HR03006). TruDiagnostic generated the DNAm and proteomic data. This research was supported in part by the Intramural Research Program of the NIH. The contributions of the NIH author(s) were made as part of their official duties as NIH federal employees, are in compliance with agency policy requirements, and are considered Works of the US Government. However, the findings and conclusions presented in this paper are those of the authors and do not necessarily reflect the views of the NIH or the US Department of Health and Human Services."}]}]},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"App1","attributes":{"class":"app"},"children":[{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"Sec37","children":[{"tag":"h3","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Extended data"}]}]}]},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"notes1","children":[{"tag":"h2","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title","data-anchor-id":"notes1"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"id":"notes1-anchor","attributes":{"data-anchor-id":"notes1","class":"usa-anchor"}},{"tag":"#text","text":"Author contributions"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Q.C. had full access to the MGB-ABC data and verified the data integrity and accuracy of the analysis. V.B.D. had access to the omics data and the TruDiagnostic Cohort and verified the data integrity and accuracy of the analysis. Conceived and designed the study: J.L.-S., R. Smith and V.B.D. Sample selection: S.H.C., R.S.K., Y.C. and S.B. Performed analysis of physical samples from Research Patient Data Registry: Y.C., S.B., A.D., M.M., C.E.W. and E.A.M. Funding support of omics: A.D., M.M., C.E.W., E.M., J.L.-S. and R. Smith. Performed analysis of physical samples for the TruDiagnostic cohort: T.M. and H.W. Data processing and normalization: Q.C., V.B.D., K.M. and P.K. Algorithm development: Q.C., V.B.D. and J.L.-S. Statistical analysis and validation: Q.C., V.B.D. and N.C.-G. Validation analyses in the Generation Scotland cohort: R.E.M. and A.R. Validation in All of Us: Q.C. and M.A.A. All authors drafted and edited the paper."}]}]},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"notes2","children":[{"tag":"h2","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title","data-anchor-id":"notes2"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"id":"notes2-anchor","attributes":{"data-anchor-id":"notes2","class":"usa-anchor"}},{"tag":"#text","text":"Peer review"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"FPar3","children":[{"tag":"h3","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Peer review information"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"id":"Par66","children":[{"tag":"em","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Nature Aging"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" thanks Daniel Belsky and the other, anonymous, reviewer(s) for their contribution to the peer review of this work."}]}]}]},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"notes3","children":[{"tag":"h2","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title","data-anchor-id":"notes3"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"id":"notes3-anchor","attributes":{"data-anchor-id":"notes3","class":"usa-anchor"}},{"tag":"#text","text":"Data availability"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"The data used in this study were generated from two biobank cohorts housed at MGB and TruDiagnostic, respectively. Requests for raw data, analyzed data and materials used in MGB and TruDiagnostic Biobank cohorts to generate the results in this study will be reviewed by the contact PIs (J.L.-S. or V.B.D.). Due to participant consent restrictions, individual-level data linked to electronic health records cannot be made publicly available. However, we are committed to supporting scientific collaboration and transparency wherever possible. Researchers interested in noncommercial academic use of the data, algorithms or derived biomarkers are encouraged to contact the corresponding author (J.L.-S.) or first author (V.B.D., varun@trudiagnostic.com). Upon review, a collaborative agreement or data use agreement can be established to enable:"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"• Access to de-identified omics data for research purposes"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"• Application of algorithms or generation of derived biomarker scores on external datasets"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"• Internal use of electronic health record-linked clinical data for validation, replication or joint analyses with external collaborators"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Requests will be assessed to determine whether they are subject to intellectual property or confidentiality obligations. Access to certain raw or analyzed data may be restricted if it relates to ongoing or future patent filings, or if release could compromise the commercialization strategy of MGB or TruDiagnostic. Access may also be limited for data containing proprietary algorithms or other commercially sensitive information. We welcome such requests and aim to respond within 30 days."}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Publicly available datasets referenced in this study include:"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"• All of Us Research Program: "},{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"attributes":{"href":"https://allofus.nih.gov/","class":"usa-link","data-ga-action":"click_feat_suppl","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"https://allofus.nih.gov/"}]}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"• Generation Scotland: "},{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"attributes":{"href":"https://genscot.ed.ac.uk/","class":"usa-link usa-link--external","data-ga-action":"click_feat_suppl","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"https://genscot.ed.ac.uk/"}]}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"• SEER proteomics data for the MGB-ABC cohort are available under PRIDE accession "},{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"attributes":{"href":"http://proteomecentral.proteomexchange.org/cgi/GetDataset?ID=PXD048709","class":"usa-link usa-link--external","data-ga-action":"click_feat_suppl","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"PXD048709"}]}]}]},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"notes4","children":[{"tag":"h2","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title","data-anchor-id":"notes4"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"id":"notes4-anchor","attributes":{"data-anchor-id":"notes4","class":"usa-anchor"}},{"tag":"#text","text":"Code availability"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Code to calculate all metrics is accessible via TruDiagnostic’s DNAm Analysis Software. You can request access to the software at "},{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"attributes":{"href":"https://www.trudiagnostic.com/softwarerequest/","class":"usa-link usa-link--external","data-ga-action":"click_feat_suppl","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"https://www.trudiagnostic.com/softwarerequest/"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":", at no cost for research purposes. Access is contingent upon the requestor agreeing to a standard, noncommercial software license agreement that confirms the intended use is strictly for academic, nonprofit research and that the requestor will not attempt to reverse engineer or commercially exploit the software. All R codes used to develop and validate EMRAge, DNAmEMRAge and OMICmAge are available at "},{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"attributes":{"href":"https://github.com/LaskySuLab/OMICmAge/","class":"usa-link usa-link--external","data-ga-action":"click_feat_suppl","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"https://github.com/LaskySuLab/OMICmAge/"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"."}]}]},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"FPar4","children":[{"tag":"h2","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title","data-anchor-id":"FPar4"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"id":"FPar4-anchor","attributes":{"data-anchor-id":"FPar4","class":"usa-anchor"}},{"tag":"#text","text":"Competing interests"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"id":"Par67","children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"This work was completed under a sponsored research agreement between Brigham Women’s Hospital and TruDiagnostic. N.C.-G., L.B.D., I.G., R.D., D.P., A.T.H.-C., S.V., S.H., T.M., R. Sehgal and V.B.D. are employees of TruDiagnostic. J.L.-S. is a scientific advisor to TruDiagnostic, Precision and Ahara. R.E.M. is a scientific advisor to the Epigenetic Clock Development Foundation and Optima Partners. J.L.-S., Q.C., V.B.D. and R. Smith have filed patents on work from this publication. M.M. and V.N.G. have filed patents on measuring cellular aging. S.T.W. receives royalties from UpToDate and is on the Board of Histolix, a digital pathology company. R.E.M. is a scientific advisor to the Epigenetic Clock Development Foundation and Optima Partners. R. Sehgal is a scientific advisor for TruDiagnostic and has received consulting fees from the company. TruDiagnostic generated the DNAm and proteomic data. Investigators from TruDiagnostic co-analyzed and co-wrote the paper as described in the contributions above. The other authors declare no competing interests."}]}]},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"fn-group1","attributes":{"class":"fn-group"},"children":[{"tag":"h2","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title","data-anchor-id":"fn-group1"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"id":"fn-group1-anchor","attributes":{"data-anchor-id":"fn-group1","class":"usa-anchor"}},{"tag":"#text","text":"Footnotes"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"fn-group p font-secondary-light font-sm"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"id":"fn1","attributes":{"class":"fn p"},"children":[{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"strong","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Publisher’s note"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" Springer Nature remains neutral with regard to jurisdictional claims in published maps and institutional affiliations."}]}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"id":"fn2","attributes":{"class":"fn p"},"children":[{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"These authors contributed equally: Qingwen Chen, Varun B. Dwaraka."}]}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"}]}]},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"sec40","children":[{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"FPar1","children":[{"tag":"h3","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Extended data"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"id":"Par64","children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"is available for this paper at 10.1038/s43587-026-01073-7."}]}]},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"FPar2","children":[{"tag":"h3","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Supplementary information"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"id":"Par65","children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"The online version contains supplementary material available at 10.1038/s43587-026-01073-7."}]}]}]},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"Bib1","attributes":{"class":"ref-list"},"children":[{"tag":"h2","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"pmc_sec_title","data-anchor-id":"Bib1"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"id":"Bib1-anchor","attributes":{"data-anchor-id":"Bib1","class":"usa-anchor"}},{"tag":"#text","text":"References"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"section","hidden":false,"id":"Bib1_sec2","children":[{"tag":"ul","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"ref-list font-sm","style":"list-style-type:none"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"li","hidden":false,"id":"CR1","children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"span","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"label"},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"1."}]},{"tag":"cite","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Ferrucci, L. & Kuchel, G. A. Heterogeneity of aging: individual risk factors, mechanisms, patient priorities, and outcomes. "},{"tag":"em","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"J. Am. Geriatr. Soc."}]},{"tag":"strong","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"69"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":", 610–612 (2021).\n"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" ["},{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"attributes":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jgs.17011","class":"usa-link usa-link--external","data-ga-action":"click_feat_suppl","target":"_blank","rel":"n